From: UniXNU <unixnu@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] perf(metal): bounded 64 MiB LRU IOSurface import cache, cross-process reclaim, and surface refusal logging

Ported from Pad 8 Pro (0006-frontend-bounded-import-reclaim) onto AdrenoMetal:
1. Bounds held IOSurface imports to a 64 MiB LRU / 2 s idle ceiling (overridable via
   kern.piano_bootargs / kern.bootargs sheng-metal-import-mib= or piano-metal-import-mib=).
2. Deduplicates concurrent in-flight surface imports across threads, retries capacity failures
   (OutOfMemory / VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY / HOST_MEMORY) after synchronous reclaim +
   org.unixnu.sheng.gpu-reclaim notification (matching Turnip's DARWIN_RECLAIM_NOTIFICATION).
3. Emits rate-limited os_log_error diagnostics on refuseSurface() for WebKit.GPU / app triage.
